    <description>Fixes defects RS04-04/RS04-06 (report defects #1 and #3): rolls the per-vehicle AF_TradeInOutcome__c up to the parent Appraisal, which is the only outcome field AF_FL_Opp_CreateQuotation / AF_FL_Appraisal_RetroAddTradeInToQuote actually read. Before this flow, recording an outcome on an AppraisalItem had no effect on the parent at all, so a multi-vehicle trade-in&apos;s quotation deduction never fired (#1), and declining one vehicle out of several never changed anything (#3).

Rollup rule (business decision, confirmed 2026-09-13, REVISED 2026-09-14 per live business feedback): parent = Withdrawn only if EVERY sibling item is Withdrawn. Otherwise, the parent only reaches a settled Accepted/Declined verdict once EVERY sibling item has a decided outcome (Accepted, Declined, or Withdrawn - i.e. none still blank/In Progress); while any item is still undecided, parent = In Progress regardless of what the decided ones say. Once all items are decided: parent = Accepted if AT LEAST ONE decided item is Accepted (accepted wins over declined among decided items); parent = Declined only if none of the decided items are Accepted (i.e. all decided items are Declined, or Declined+Withdrawn with zero Accepted).

2026-09-14 change (two iterations, both from live business feedback on the same 2-item scenario): the original rule set parent=Declined the instant ANY item was set to Declined, even while the other item was still blank/undecided - so a fresh 2-item trade-in with one item just-declined and the other never touched read as a dead deal prematurely. Fixed by requiring ALL items to have a decided outcome before the parent reaches any final Accepted/Declined verdict; until then it stays In Progress. Within a fully-decided set, Accepted takes priority over Declined (1 accepted + 1 declined -&gt; Accepted, not Declined or In Progress) since at least one vehicle is still usable as a trade-in once every item has actually been evaluated.

Fires on AppraisalItem create/update whenever AF_TradeInOutcome__c changes, re-reads every sibling item fresh (not just the triggering one) so it produces the same correct parent state regardless of which vehicle changed or in what order. Bulk-safe: works off the record&apos;s own AppraisalId at the single-record RecordAfterSave level (standard record-triggered flow, not a batch), same pattern as every other AppraisalItem-triggered flow in this org (AF_FL_AppraisalItem_EvaluationComplete, AF_FL_AppraisalItem_GenerateBookInSheet).

2026-09-13 fix, found via live empirical testing of defect #3: Assign_Declined&apos;s write of Appraisal.AF_TradeInOutcome__c=&quot;Declined&quot; hit AF_VR_Appraisal_DeclineReasonRequired (LFRDN-633, pre-existing in the org), which requires AF_FinalRemarks__c whenever the outcome is Declined - this rollup flow never populated it, so declining an item threw FIELD_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_EXCEPTION and the whole update was blocked. Added Formula_DeclineRemark (references the triggering item&apos;s own Make/Model/AppraisalItemNumber) to the same update. This is a system-generated placeholder, not a real refusal reason from a human - the report&apos;s own defect #3 write-up already flags this as an open BA question (should decline reason become per-item instead of parent-level); this fix only unblocks the save, it does not resolve that open question.</description>
